{"type": "spr", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"10 x equals 86\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>10</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>86</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is the solution to the given equation?</p>", "keys": ["8.6", "43/5"], "rationale": "<p>The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8.6\"><mn>8.6</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of the given equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals 8.6\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.6</mn></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"8.6\"><mn>8.6</mn></math> is the solution to the given equation. Note that 8.6&nbsp;and 43/5&nbsp;are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>", "externalid": "c33a8ce0-debc-4709-b0d7-3f1800613186", "correct_answer": ["8.6", "43/5"]}